# Jess Bot Privacy Policy

**Effective date:** August 31, 2026  
**Last updated:** August 31, 2026

This Privacy Policy explains how the independent developer operating Jess Bot
(**Jess**, **we**, **us**, or **our**) collects, uses, stores, and shares information
when you use Jess Bot, the Jess World Discord server, or
[jessbot.xyz](https://jessbot.xyz) (together, the **Service**).

## 1. Information we process

Depending on how you use Jess, we may process:

- **Discord information:** numeric Discord user ID, server membership and roles,
  preferred language, operational timestamps, command interactions, and the information
  Discord makes available to the bot for the requested feature.
- **Conversation content:** text you send to Jess and, when supported, an image attached
  to your current message. User text is limited to 1,000 characters before it enters
  Jess's operational history, database, memory system, or AI request.
- **Conversation history and memory:** a short recent history used for conversational
  continuity; up to the last three user messages may be retained as an operational
  backup. Tier 2 and Tier 3 may also store user-authored text as isolated semantic
  memory. Tier 1 does not create semantic memory, and downgrading to Tier 1 removes that
  semantic-memory collection.
- **Subscription information:** Patreon user or member identifiers, membership tier,
  membership and charge status, relevant timestamps, refund status, and the Discord ID
  linked through Patreon. Jess does not need your full payment-card number.
- **Usage information:** daily message counts, quota dates, errors, security logs, and
  other information necessary to operate and protect the Service.
- **Referral information:** referral code, Discord user ID, invite code and join time,
  membership-conversion status, commission window, relevant Patreon charge or refund
  records, and payout-accounting status.
- **Website and attribution information:** an anonymous visitor ID, session and A/B-test
  variant, referral and campaign parameters (such as UTM values or advertising click
  identifiers), CTA destination, tier selection, consent state, and timestamps. The
  website may use first-party local or session storage for these functions.
- **Support information:** information you voluntarily provide in a support ticket or
  other communication.

The website's Discord identity connection stores the verified numeric Discord ID, not
the returned username, avatar, Discord access token, or refresh token. The Patreon
identity connection stores the verified Patreon user ID, not the user's Patreon access
token, refresh token, email address, username, or profile details. OAuth state records
are temporary and expire after approximately ten minutes.

## 2. How we use information

We use information to:

- provide AI responses, conversation continuity, memory, language, and tier features;
- verify paid access and enforce message or feature limits;
- synchronize Discord and Patreon membership status;
- attribute referrals and calculate, review, and audit partner commissions;
- operate website login, checkout routing, analytics, and conversion measurement;
- prevent abuse, investigate errors, secure accounts, and maintain the Service;
- answer support and deletion requests; and
- comply with applicable law and enforce our Terms of Service.

We do not sell your personal information.

## 3. AI processing and service providers

Relevant text and current image references may be sent to OpenAI to generate responses,
embeddings, or other AI functionality. Images are supplied using Discord-hosted URLs and
are not intentionally downloaded into Jess's local image folder.

We also rely on providers such as Discord for communication and identity, Patreon for
memberships and billing, OpenAI Sites and its infrastructure providers for the website,
Porkbun for domain and DNS administration, and database or hosting infrastructure used
to operate Jess. These providers process information under their own terms and privacy
policies. Information may be processed in countries other than yours.

## 4. Retention

We retain information only for as long as reasonably needed for the purposes above,
security, accounting, dispute resolution, and legal obligations. Current operational
practices include:

- keeping only a bounded recent conversation history in active memory;
- retaining up to three recent user messages as a restart backup;
- retaining Tier 2 and Tier 3 semantic memories until deletion, downgrade to Tier 1, or
  another applicable cleanup event;
- retaining daily usage records as needed to enforce quotas; and
- retaining referral, commission, charge, refund, and payout records as needed to avoid
  duplicate or incorrect affiliate payments and maintain an audit trail.

Backups and provider-side copies may take additional time to expire. We may retain
limited records when required by law or reasonably necessary to prevent fraud and abuse.

## 5. Sharing

We share information only as needed with service providers described above, when you
direct us to do so, to protect the rights and safety of users or the Service, during a
legitimate business or service transfer, or when required by law. Referral reports are
restricted to authorized administrators; partner accounting should expose only the
information necessary to review the relevant referral and payment.

## 6. Security

We use reasonable technical and organizational safeguards, including access controls,
per-user memory separation, authenticated synchronization, signature verification for
webhooks, and encryption for selected stored credentials. No system is completely
secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.

## 7. Your choices and rights

You may:

- stop messaging Jess or leave the Discord server;
- disconnect Discord from Patreon through the applicable account settings;
- cancel your Patreon membership through Patreon;
- ask what Jess remembers about you using available features; and
- request deletion or correction of your Jess data through the support process below.

A verified deletion request removes the user's Jess database record, semantic memory,
active history, and local caches. Some accounting, referral, security, webhook, or
payment records may be retained where reasonably necessary or legally required. Data
controlled independently by Discord, Patreon, OpenAI, or another provider must be
managed through that provider.

Depending on where you live, you may have additional rights to access, correct, delete,
restrict, object to, or receive a copy of personal information. We may need to verify
that the Discord account making a request belongs to you.

## 8. Children

The Service is not intended for anyone below Discord's minimum permitted age or the
higher minimum age required by local law. If you believe a child has provided personal
information in violation of those requirements, contact us so we can investigate and
delete it where appropriate.

## 9. Changes to this policy

We may update this Privacy Policy as the Service changes. The latest revision date will
appear at the top, and material changes may also be announced on the website or in Jess
World.

## 10. Contact and deletion requests

Join the official Jess World support server at
[discord.gg/uFSvN7nVYw](https://discord.gg/uFSvN7nVYw) and open a support ticket. State
that you are making a privacy or deletion request and identify the Discord account
concerned. Do not send passwords, bot tokens, payment-card information, or identity
documents unless we specifically explain why verification is required and provide a
safe method.

